          "params": {
            "description": "EN (Input) — Enable pin. Driving this pin to logic high enables the device; driving this pin to logic low or floating this pin disables the device. This pin features an internal pulldown resistor, which is disconnected when EN is driven high externally and the device has started up.",
            "source": "https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps7a02.pdf (§5 Table 5-1 Pin Functions, DBV column)"
          },
          "type": "pin_functions"
        },
        {
          "params": {
            "note": "Active high: VEN(HI) >= 1.1 V enables, VEN(LOW) <= 0.3 V disables. Floating EN is held low by the 500 kohm smart pulldown, which is disconnected once EN is driven high and the device has started. EN leakage 10 nA at 6 V. EN toggle frequency 10 kHz max. If independent control is not needed, connect EN to IN.",
            "source": "https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps7a02.pdf (§6.3, §6.5, §7.3.4)"
          },
          "type": "usage_note"
