      "traits": [
        {
          "params": {
            "note": "Fixed 1.8 V: ±1 % at 25 C, ±1.5 % over TJ -40 to 125 C. Line regulation 5 mV max; load regulation (1-200 mA) 20 mV typ / 38 mV max at TJ -40 to 85 C, 50 mV max at -40 to 125 C. 0-200 mA continuous. Current limit ICL 240 / 450 / 750 mA (min / typ / max, tested at VIN = VOUT(nom) + VDO(max) + 1.0 V for VOUT < 2.5 V), brick-wall above VFOLDBACK = 0.5 V and foldback below it to ISC 65 mA typ into a short; thermal shutdown 170 C, reset 145 C. PSRR 55 dB at 1 kHz. Start-up (EN to 90 % VOUT) 750 us typ / 1200 us max.",
            "source": "https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps7a02.pdf (§6.3, §6.5, §6.6, §7.3.6, §7.3.8)"
          },
          "type": "usage_note"
        },
        {
          "params": {
            "note": "COUT 1-22 uF ceramic (1 uF nominal); at least 0.5 uF effective capacitance is required for stability and 22 uF is the largest derated value. Place it as close to OUT as possible.",
            "source": "https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps7a02.pdf (§5, §6.3, §8.1.2, §8.4.1)"
          },
          "type": "usage_note"
        },
        {
          "params": {
            "note": "Active output discharge (P version): when disabled by EN or UVLO, OUT is pulled to ground through RPULLDOWN = 60 ohm (VIN 3.3 V). Do not rely on it to discharge a large output capacitance after the input has collapsed: reverse current from OUT to IN may flow; limit it to 5 % of the rated current for a short time.",
            "source": "https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps7a02.pdf (§6.5, §7.3.2, §7.4.4)"
          },
          "type": "usage_note"
        }
      ]
